{"id":"word:hebrew:H817","type":"word","title":"אָשָׁם","subtitle":"H817 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"guilt ; by implication, a fault ; also a sin-offering","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אָשָׁם (H817) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 46 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אָשָׁם (ʼâshâm) means guilt ; by implication, a fault ; also a sin-offering First listed occurrence: 1Sam 6 3."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אָשָׁם","transliteration":"ʼâshâm","pronunciation":"aw-shawm'","strong":"H817","lemmaId":"hebrew:H817","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["אָשָׁ֖ם","הָ/אָשָׁ֖ם","לְ/אָשָׁ֖ם","אָשָׁ֑ם","אָשָׁ֔ם"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncmsa",15],["HNcmsa",12],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",6],["HR/Ncmsa",5],["HC/Td/Ncmsa",3],["HC/Rd/Ncmsa",2],["HRd/Ncmsa",1],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",1],["HR/Ncmpc/Sp3ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"guilt ; by implication, a fault ; also a sin-offering","usage":"guiltiness, (offering for) sin, trespass (offering).","full":"H817. asham אָשָׁם noun masculine offence, guilt — ׳א Gen 26:10 37t., suffix אֲשָׁמוֺ Num 5:7 7 t.; — 1 offence, trespass, fault Psa 68:22 ( guiltiness RV). 2 guilt Gen 26:10 (J) Prov 14:9 ; Jer 51:5 . 3 compensation , אֵלָיו הָאָשָׁם לְהָשִׁיב to whom to return the compensation (or satisfaction for injury) Num 5:7-8 , (P; restitution for guilt RV). 4 trespass-offering (AV, but guilt-offering RV) used only in Leviticus 5; Lev 6:10 ; 7:1 ; 14:1 ; 19:21-22 , Num 5:1 ; 6:12 ; 18:9 (P), & Ezek 40:39 ; 42:13 ; 44:29 ; 46:20 , compare Ezra 10:19 . This offering seems to have been confined to offences against God or man that could be estimated and so covered by compensation. The ordinary trespass-offering was a ram, together with restitution and a penalty of a fifth of its value. The trespass-offerings of the leper and Nazirite were he-lambs Leviticus 14 Num 6:12 ; if the person who suffered wrong or his kinsmen were not living the fine went to the priests. The victims were offered, the blood and fat pieces going to the altar, the skin and flesh to the priests. There seems to have been no application of the blood to the horns of the altar (the chief ceremony of the sin-offering) because the guilt was not expiated at the altar but by compensation to the wronged person or his representative. A part of the blood of the leper's trespass-offering was applied to his person to consecrate him (as in the case of the ram of consecration to consecrate the priests Lev 8:23 ). The trespass-offering is unknown to J E D and the older Hebrew literature. However, the Philistines send an אשׁם of golden mice and tumours 1Sam 6:3-4 , 8 , 17 , and an אשׁם of money was given to the priests 2Kin 12:17 , but these are entirely different from the trespass-offering of P. The Messianic servant offers himself as an אשׁם in compensation for the sins of the people, interposing for them as their substitute Isa 53:10 (incorrectly, sin-offering AV RV). See further Oehler OT Theol. § 137 Di Lev 5:14 .","rootNote":"from 816 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 6 3","keyReferences":["1Sam 6 3","1Sam 6 4","1Sam 6 8","1Sam 6 17","2Kgs 12 17","Ezek 40 39","Ezek 42 13","Ezek 44 29"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":46,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 6 3","book":"1Sam","chapter":6,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אָשָׁ֑ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 6 4","book":"1Sam","chapter":6,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אָשָׁם֮","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 6 8","book":"1Sam","chapter":6,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אָשָׁ֔ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 6 17","book":"1Sam","chapter":6,"verse":17,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אָשָׁ֖ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":